node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
.DS_Store
.vite
tools/render-studio

# Object-storage credentials. Covered by *.local above, but named explicitly so
# narrowing that glob can never silently expose keys. A key that reaches a public
# repo is compromised even after removal — git keeps history and forks keep copies.
# If it ever happens: ROTATE the key, do not just delete the line.
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Verbatim prompt log, written by the log-prompt hook. This repo is PUBLIC, and
# this file accumulates everything typed to the assistant. The rest of memory/ IS
# tracked — decisions and lessons benefit from history; a transcript does not.
memory/user-prompts.md

# Project media lives in Cloudflare R2 (bucket chandparaaa-media), not in git.
# src/data/media-manifest.json is what the build reads; it IS tracked. These
# files stay on disk locally so `npm run dev` works offline and the manifest can
# be regenerated, but they are never committed again.
# Re-sync with:  npm run media:sync && npm run media:verify
public/projects/
